                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef8ea4a0-8cd6-3f04-99f3-1c1fa376ae86",
                        "entry_id": "6fce1760-1866-355b-8e51-bec0b3a630c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Hypothetically, to undo the act of rape; to cause (a person) not to have been raped."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2953971-1719-49c4-a158-80c5eddf2b67",
                                "sense_id": "ef8ea4a0-8cd6-3f04-99f3-1c1fa376ae86",
                                "text": "I could not unoppress all those women; I could not resurrect all the murdered witches; I could not unrape all the little girls."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fd898fa-13ef-40fc-9a21-5d43b4c8f238",
                                "sense_id": "ef8ea4a0-8cd6-3f04-99f3-1c1fa376ae86",
                                "text": "In fact, experience has demonstrated that “abortion does not unrape a woman,” and it “promises only to compound the trauma of rape with another experience of violence.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d53f695-4ee2-434c-a557-302a919fd712",
                                "sense_id": "ef8ea4a0-8cd6-3f04-99f3-1c1fa376ae86",
                                "text": "To illustrate with a crude parallel, the idea is the following: that one cannot unmurder the murdered and that one cannot unrape the raped."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
